instruction:
Review this Java code for security vulnerabilities:
```java
File f = new File("/uploads/" + request.getParameter("file"));
return new FileInputStream(f);
```

output:
**Path Traversal** (CWE-22) [HIGH]

Validate canonical path to prevent traversal.

**Vulnerable code:**
```java
File f = new File("/uploads/" + request.getParameter("file"));
return new FileInputStream(f);
```

**Fixed code:**
```java
String name = new File(request.getParameter("file")).getName();
File f = new File("/uploads", name);
if (!f.getCanonicalPath().startsWith(new File("/uploads").getCanonicalPath())) throw new SecurityException();
return new FileInputStream(f);
```

