instruction:
Review this JavaScript code for security vulnerabilities:
```javascript
app.post("/api/delete-account", (req, res) => {
  User.deleteOne({ _id: req.session.userId });
  res.json({ ok: true });
});
```

output:
**Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)** (CWE-352) [MEDIUM]

Add CSRF middleware to state-changing routes.

**Vulnerable code:**
```javascript
app.post("/api/delete-account", (req, res) => {
  User.deleteOne({ _id: req.session.userId });
  res.json({ ok: true });
});
```

**Fixed code:**
```javascript
const csrf = require("csurf");
app.use(csrf({ cookie: true }));

app.post("/api/delete-account", (req, res) => {
  User.deleteOne({ _id: req.session.userId });
  res.json({ ok: true });
});
```

